# Examples of .changescriberc configurations

## Simple Configuration (Recommended)

### GitHub Issues

If your files follow the pattern: `projectname-123.md` (e.g., `theater-unity3d-34.md`)

```json
{
  "generate": {
    "fromPackageJson": true,
    "excludeTaskList": false,
    "issueSystem": "github",
    "taskUrlTemplate": "https://github.com/your-org/{project}/issues/{taskCode}"
  }
}
```

**How it works:**
- File: `theater-unity3d-34.md` → project: `theater-unity3d`, issue: `34`
- Generated link: `https://github.com/your-org/theater-unity3d/issues/34`
- No need to specify regex pattern!

### Jira Issues

If your files follow the pattern: `KALI-123.md` (project code already in filename)

```json
{
  "generate": {
    "fromPackageJson": true,
    "excludeTaskList": false,
    "issueSystem": "jira",
    "taskUrlTemplate": "https://yourdomain.atlassian.net/browse/{taskCode}"
  }
}
```

**How it works:**
- File: `KALI-123.md` → taskCode: `KALI-123`
- Generated link: `https://yourdomain.atlassian.net/browse/KALI-123`

### GitLab Issues

If your files follow the pattern: `myproject-456.md`

```json
{
  "generate": {
    "fromPackageJson": true,
    "excludeTaskList": false,
    "issueSystem": "gitlab",
    "taskUrlTemplate": "https://gitlab.com/your-org/{project}/-/issues/{taskCode}"
  }
}
```

**How it works:**
- File: `myproject-456.md` → project: `myproject`, issue: `456`
- Generated link: `https://gitlab.com/your-org/myproject/-/issues/456`

---

## Advanced Configuration (Custom Patterns)

If you need a custom pattern not covered by the predefined `issueSystem` options, you can use `taskCodePattern`:

### Custom Pattern Example

```json
{
  "generate": {
    "fromPackageJson": true,
    "taskCodePattern": "^([A-Z]+-\\d+)",
    "taskUrlTemplate": "https://example.com/issue/{taskCode}"
  }
}
```

**Pattern explanation:**
- `^([A-Z]+-\\d+)`: Matches uppercase letters, dash, and numbers at the start
- Extracts "PROJ-123" from "PROJ-123-description.md"

**Note:** `taskCodePattern` overrides `issueSystem` if both are specified.

## Advanced Pattern Examples

### Extract issue number from anywhere in filename
Pattern: `issue-(\\d+)` for files like "feature-issue-789.md"

```json
{
  "generate": {
    "taskCodePattern": "issue-(\\d+)"
  }
}
```

### Extract prefix and number
Pattern: `^([A-Z]+-\\d+)` for files like "FEAT-123-description.md"

```json
{
  "generate": {
    "taskCodePattern": "^([A-Z]+-\\d+)"
  }
}
```

### No pattern (default behavior)
Uses the full filename without extension as taskCode

```json
{
  "generate": {
    "fromPackageJson": true,
    "taskUrlTemplate": "https://example.com/task/{taskCode}"
  }
}
```
